1562 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The Creminicap are the most commonly encountered of all Fungrown\056 These small\054 dome\055topped creatures typically are not found in exclusive\054 isolated colonies\056 Rather\054 they prefer to intermingle with other species of Fungrown\056 More adventurous Creminicap have been known to integrate into societies in Highpeak\054 Essex\054 and other areas in Pliara\056 They will often find work performing difficult manual labor\054 making deliveries\054 or working as assistants to mages\056\n\nCreminicap are relatively docile in nature and extremely co\055dependent\056 Finding a lone Creminicap is such a rarity that it would typically be an indication that the Creminicap may be lost or hurt\056 Even when looking to join a new colony or integrate into a new society\054 the Creminicap never travels alone\056 There is often a group of at least 3 Creminicap\054 although seeing two alone is not uncommon\056\n\nCreminicap love to work and enjoy feeling as though they are productive members of their society\056 Carpentry and shipbuilding are common hobbies of the Creminicap\054 while many others will delve into the magical arts\056 It is uncommon\054 although not unheard of\054 to wander across a Creminicap of the bardic or divine arts\054 however\056\n\nStanding around 3 feet tall\054 the Creminicap is very short\054 but well\055built for hard work\056 They have the ability to force their outermost layers to shed on occasion\054 freeing them from any disease or poison that may have entered their bodies\056 Their thicker layers give them a little more cushion in absorbing damage\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 1563 0 R
     /Pg 1540 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1563 0 obj
  << /K [ 1562 0 R ]
