1568 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Morelcap are native primarily to swamps\054 marshes\054 and other areas with a lot of moisture\056 Easily identified by the spongey\054 cone\055shaped cap on their heads\054 Morelcap are excellent swimmers that can even outswim many aquatic creatures\056\n\nUnlike the Creminicap\054 the Morelcap prefer to isolate themselves from the rest of the world and are often found living in colonies consisting solely of Morelcap\056 There have been notable instances\054 however\054 such as the Waterspore Troop in the Essex Marshlands\054 where Morelcap have formed complex societies with other species and races\056\n\nAlthough generally peaceful and compassionate in nature\054 a Morelcap will fight to the death to protect its home\054 family\054 and loved ones\056 While still smaller than the titanic Armillacap\054 the Morelcap stand an average of 4\0476\042 tall\073 around a full foot taller than Creminicap or Amanitacap\056)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 1569 0 R
     /Pg 1540 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

