1576 0 obj
  << /ActualText (To the scholars of Pliara\054 civilization is measured in stone\054 steel\054 and written law\054 achievements that place the Dwarves as the first true people of the world\056 To the Fungrown\054 those mountain halls and library stacks are merely recent additions to an ancient landscape\056 Living mushroom folk of small to medium stature\054 the Fungrown carry a deep conviction that their roots reach back to the morning of creation\056 They believe that when Plii first spoke life into the flora and fauna\054 they sprouted alongside it\054 making them the true firstborn of Pliara\056\n\nOutsiders rarely grant them that history\054 often dismissing them as simple forest wanderers or spitting the derogatory term Sporite to paint them as mere pests\056 Yet to walk among the Fungrown is to encounter a culture completely integrated with the natural world\056 They have no need for massive fortresses or grand empires\056 Their communities thrive in the damp shadow of ancient canopies\054 quiet riverbanks\054 and forgotten caves\056 While they lack the rigid structures of dwarven clans\054 their heritage lives on through oral traditions\054 shared instincts\054 and an enduring connection to the soil beneath their feet\056\n\nPhysically\054 no two Fungrown look identical\054 but all are instantly recognizable by the prominent fungal cap topping their heads\056 Beneath these broad crowns are sturdy\054 fibrous bodies built for survival\056 They do not view the world through the short urgency of mortals\054 nor do they share common attitudes about personal property\056 Instead\054 a Fungrown moves through life with a distinct focus on purpose\054 whether that means tending a quiet grove for decades or venturing out into chaotic cities out of unquenchable curiosity\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 1577 0 R
     /Pg 1542 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1577 0 obj
  << /K [ 1576 0 R ]
     /P 1580 0 R
     /S /P
